.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBHistogramRange\fR: a histogram that doubles as a range picker. Bars inside the selected range are accented and the others dimmed. Pressing a bar selects that bin's range.
.PP
The distribution shows where values cluster, which two bare thumbs cannot. Put a \fBRangeSlider\fR under it for the exact thumbs; the pair is the example for \fBComposedComponent\fR.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.TP
.B HistogramRange::new(histogram: &'a Histogram, selection: (f32, f32), on_pick: impl Fn((f32, f32)) \-> M + 'a)
\fBselection\fR is the chosen \fB(lo, hi)\fR; \fBon_pick\fR gets a bin's range when its bar is pressed.
